VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '54 looks. 54. Different energy, different contexts. Casual, put together. I could do even better than this, but we\'re looking for range. The more you give it, the better results you can get. From inside your avatar, you\'ve'

[01:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'got two paths for adding more. You can upload footage or photos directly, or you can ask AI to design a new look entirely. We\'re looking to upload first and I want to tell you why. When you give HeyGen more source material, more angles, more lighting conditions, more'

[01:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of you, it has more to work with. That makes your AI generated looks more accurate, more natural, and closer to what you\'re actually going for. You\'re not just adding a look, you are improving everything that comes after it. Inside your avatar, click to add'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'more looks. You\'ve got a few ways to get footage in. Drag and drop, record directly, or paste a Google Drive link. HeyGen gives you tips right here. If uploading a video, speak expressively for at least 15 seconds. [music] I'

[01:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'suggest more. Natural expressions and gestures. Pause between sentences. Quiet, well-lit space. Same setup that gave you a great clone gives you great additional looks. Photos work, too, and this is where I want to spend a second.'

[02:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'HeyGen is very clear about what it needs. One person in the photo only, face clearly visible. HeyGen shows you the do\'s and don\'ts right here. And the don\'ts are things that seem fine at first. A group photo where you\'re in it. A shot where your face is cut off on the'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'edge. But don\'t do it. You\'re just asking for trouble. A clean solo shot where you can see your gorgeous face clearly? Yes. Do that. I\'ve uploaded a lot of reference photos, and you can see it in the quality of what comes out.'

[02:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Every upload is an investment in every video you make from here forward. Do a few before you move on to the AI path, and you will notice a difference. Now that you\'ve given HeyGen more to work with, we can make videos using any of'

[02:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'these images as looks, but first, let\'s go design something. Back in your avatar, let\'s choose design with AI. You describe what you want. You can add visual references, and it creates a new look for your avatar based on that'

[02:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'input. The references part is the thing most people don\'t think to use, but it\'s the key to getting results that are way better than just trying to describe what you\'re thinking. Your current look is on the left. That\'s the base HeyGen is'

[03:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'starting from. The text field is where you describe the edit. And see this toggle on the right, personal model. Make sure that is on. That tells HeyGen to use your face and not just a generic stand-in. Now, references. Click that.'

[03:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is where you upload photos or videos to show HeyGen what you\'re going for, not just describing it, actually showing it. A photo of a setting that you love, a screenshot of an aesthetic you want to match, a picture of yourself'

[03:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in the environment you want the look to reflect. This is how I got the version of my avatar in the car with an iced coffee. I gave HeyGen a reference of the exact context. You\'ve seen these types of videos, casual chatting in the car. I'

[03:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'found some screenshots, then I uploaded them. And because I already uploaded additional looks of myself before I got here, it had a stronger foundation to build from. Reference uploaded, description written, now we generate.'

